WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:03.640
Giemon of Inarizaka has been beheaded again!

00:03.640 --> 00:07.000
It doesn't matter how many times they kill him.

00:07.060 --> 00:09.350
He'll just come back to life again.

00:09.430 --> 00:10.520
Giemon isn't a person. He's a Kowai.

00:10.470 --> 00:11.800
Kowai! Kowai!

00:12.460 --> 00:13.500
Ogin-san?

00:14.660 --> 00:16.540
Do you still intend to live?

00:24.080 --> 00:32.850
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:32.890 --> 00:41.890
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

00:41.930 --> 00:48.660
Constantly searching,
still can't find

00:51.270 --> 00:57.340
Ever illusive peace of mind

00:59.510 --> 01:08.080
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:08.120 --> 01:14.720
And I'm faced with another day

01:15.930 --> 01:21.660
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:21.700 --> 01:26.000
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:26.040 --> 01:30.480
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:30.510 --> 01:34.910
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:34.950 --> 01:39.440
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:39.490 --> 01:47.330
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

01:49.170 --> 01:49.200
Kowai

01:57.190 --> 01:58.400
Yeah, it's true.

01:58.860 --> 02:01.280
Even if he dies, he just comes back to life.

02:02.400 --> 02:06.280
This'll be the third time that Giemen
of Inarizaka has had his head chopped off.

02:06.740 --> 02:07.740
The third time?

02:08.540 --> 02:10.790
He'll probably revive this time as well.

02:11.290 --> 02:12.250
That's...

02:12.620 --> 02:14.540
The first time was fifteen years ago.

02:14.710 --> 02:16.540
The second, five years ago.

02:16.840 --> 02:19.300
Everybody in the underground knows about it.

02:19.800 --> 02:22.380
He's a genuine monster.

02:22.970 --> 02:27.050
Just what kind of connection is
there between Ogin-san and that monster?

02:27.600 --> 02:31.390
Giemon of Inarizaka killed Ogin's parents.

02:31.430 --> 02:32.020
What?

02:33.100 --> 02:35.640
She may intend to avenge them all by herself.

02:35.940 --> 02:39.020
But this one's a bad one to go up against, sensei.

02:40.280 --> 02:41.150
Mr. Retiree?

02:43.190 --> 02:45.650
Jeez, I've been calling you for a while!

02:45.910 --> 02:48.370
Oh, it's you, Orikudon.

02:48.780 --> 02:49.830
Has something happened?

02:50.410 --> 02:52.790
The book renter, Heihachi-san, is here to see you.

02:53.330 --> 02:56.500
Oh, Heihachi-san? I guess he's back in Edo.

02:57.630 --> 02:59.340
Yup. Got back three days ago.

03:02.960 --> 03:05.630
I had a lot of deliveries to
make, so I got delayed for five days.

03:06.130 --> 03:09.350
Thanks to that, I missed the
execution everybody has been talking about.

03:11.100 --> 03:15.310
The execution of one of the worst
villains in the world, Giemon of Inarizaka.

03:15.640 --> 03:17.190
You saw it, didn't you, Momosuke-san?

03:17.440 --> 03:20.940
Well, yes... My publisher,
Tsutaya-san, whipped me into going.

03:21.400 --> 03:23.820
"If youre collecting kaidan, go see it," he said.

03:24.690 --> 03:27.400
But, isn't his decapitated head still on display?

03:27.910 --> 03:29.660
What, haven't you heard?

03:29.950 --> 03:31.910
It disappeared three days ago!

03:32.620 --> 03:33.490
What did you say?

03:34.000 --> 03:36.580
Jeez, you miss out because you're always cooped up!

03:37.170 --> 03:39.120
Some say they saw it flying in the sky,

03:39.250 --> 03:42.710
and some even say that fire was coming out of its eyes!

03:42.840 --> 03:46.510
Still, I just can't bring myself to
believe that a person would come back to life!

03:46.720 --> 03:48.550
Well then, let's go take a look!

03:49.470 --> 03:51.760
This is the third day since the head has disappeared.

03:52.850 --> 03:57.850
Everybody's wondering if Giemon will appear
at Inarizaka now that he has come back to life.

03:58.310 --> 04:00.650
Edo sure is great, isn't it?

04:00.730 --> 04:04.150
How should I say it... There's a smell
that says a lot of people are living here.

04:04.400 --> 04:07.320
For me... it's slightly uncomfortable.

04:07.700 --> 04:10.820
Even though everyone lives each day to the utmost, I...

04:15.700 --> 04:20.370
Say, sensei... If your world,
which you'd been taking for granted until yesterday,

04:20.830 --> 04:24.250
was utterly destroyed in a
single night and became living hell,

04:24.670 --> 04:26.590
how would you feel?

04:27.130 --> 04:32.340
Ogin felt that when she was but
an innocent little girl with pigtails.

04:33.140 --> 04:35.120
Konoeya

04:33.140 --> 04:35.120
Konoeya

04:34.430 --> 04:38.020
Well, we are sorry about the robbery, Onaegi.

04:38.180 --> 04:40.140
But this is a business matter for us.

04:40.850 --> 04:42.610
Please wait just a little longer...

04:42.810 --> 04:46.940
If we sell the shop, how are we supposed to make a living?

04:55.580 --> 04:56.370
What's your name?

04:57.000 --> 04:57.540
Chiyo.

04:58.200 --> 04:59.580
Ah, little Chiyo.

05:00.080 --> 05:03.080
Did you see the face of the
robber who murdered your father?

05:06.500 --> 05:08.210
He was wearing a black hood.

05:08.470 --> 05:11.260
He dragged my father into a storeroom...

05:11.510 --> 05:13.180
And then, the storeroom caught fire...

05:14.260 --> 05:17.390
The sake caught fire, and... and...

05:17.680 --> 05:20.390
He took advantage of the commotion and fled, is that it?

05:26.020 --> 05:27.570
Look deep into its eyes...

05:29.240 --> 05:30.440
You must've been scared...

05:31.280 --> 05:34.570
But you don't have to remember any of this anymore.

05:38.750 --> 05:42.330
See? The fear is gone from your mind.

05:43.040 --> 05:46.250
There's no need to be afraid of your dreams anymore.

05:47.670 --> 05:52.220
Sensei, there are true demons in this world.

05:55.140 --> 05:58.010
Huh? Nobody is here, eh?

05:58.720 --> 06:03.390
I thought there'd at least be a few
curious visitors since everyone is talking about it.

06:03.560 --> 06:06.310
In the end, people are afraid of monsters.

06:08.070 --> 06:10.480
Nothing's going to happen while
we're standing out here in the open.

06:10.860 --> 06:12.700
Let's go watch from those shadows. This way!

06:13.860 --> 06:15.360
Wait, Heihachi-san!

06:20.870 --> 06:22.910
Nothing has appeared...

06:23.210 --> 06:23.960
Yeah...

06:24.460 --> 06:26.170
Shall we head back?

06:26.420 --> 06:28.460
Yes, let's.

06:34.340 --> 06:35.630
I-It's here!

06:36.800 --> 06:39.560
Oh, so we weren't alone, after all.

06:39.680 --> 06:42.730
[Note: Kitsunebi - Fox fire.]

06:39.680 --> 06:40.510
It's a kitsunebi!

06:40.680 --> 06:41.560
Save me!

06:43.100 --> 06:44.440
It's getting closer!

06:44.770 --> 06:45.810
R-Right.

06:49.860 --> 06:54.320
[Note: Mononoke - supernatural entities like youkai.]

06:49.860 --> 06:54.320
You accursed mononoke, I shall dispose of you!

07:00.290 --> 07:04.460
That's the man who caught Giemon,
Genzou Sasamori-sama of Kitamachi!

07:07.630 --> 07:08.460
Ogin-san?

07:09.840 --> 07:11.840
[Sign: Kyougokutei]

07:12.300 --> 07:16.840
So you were the one who used a fake letter to
bring sensei back to Edo when he was in Kyoto?

07:17.840 --> 07:22.220
Didn't your last setup work well thanks to him?

07:22.310 --> 07:24.220
That's true.

07:24.390 --> 07:31.860
You weren't thinking of parting ways
with that sensei, were you, Mataichi-san?

07:32.280 --> 07:35.530
He's not someone who is capable of living in the darkness.

07:35.610 --> 07:40.030
I feel that the time when lightness and
darkness can live separately is drawing to an end.

07:40.870 --> 07:43.830
All people possess darkness in their hearts.

07:44.450 --> 07:49.250
It is because they try to repress the darkness by force that
these strange and mysterious things are rife in this world.

07:45.120 --> 07:51.000
[Sign: Kyougokutei]

07:49.710 --> 07:51.000
To begin with...

07:51.540 --> 07:52.750
"To begin with"?

07:53.050 --> 07:56.300
There is nothing mysterious in this world.

07:56.720 --> 07:58.300
Isn't that right?

07:58.890 --> 08:01.100
Just what are you planning?

08:03.100 --> 08:06.020
You haven't forgotten, have you, Komatakugun?

08:06.100 --> 08:08.520
You haven't forgotten who makes it
possible for you to live in this world, have you?

08:08.850 --> 08:11.690
It's not as though I'm in this
world because I am attached to it.

08:12.650 --> 08:20.160
Anyway, shall we do as we always have...
make use of him when he can be useful?

08:27.870 --> 08:30.500
Boss Giemon came back to life again!

08:30.750 --> 08:31.920
R-Really?

08:32.040 --> 08:34.250
The Boss just sent out an order!

08:34.590 --> 08:39.510
Yeah he did; he told us to follow the policeman
from Kitamachi who caught him, Genzou Sasamori!

08:40.140 --> 08:41.970
Giemon is a Kowai.

08:42.390 --> 08:45.100
Those who are greedy and can't cast aside
their obsession with the world of the living

08:45.350 --> 08:48.810
come back to life upon death and
become a monster called a "Kowai."

08:49.270 --> 08:51.310
They say Giemon is alive again?

08:54.980 --> 08:57.230
Nonsense... he's dead.

08:57.610 --> 09:00.650
There must be someone
who's trying to set up a trap for me.

09:15.750 --> 09:16.920
What's wrong?

09:17.710 --> 09:20.260
You're not drinking at all, Sasamori-dono.

09:20.630 --> 09:21.680
Err, well...

09:21.800 --> 09:23.220
Come, drink up.

09:25.220 --> 09:26.350
Hey, Sasamori!

09:35.230 --> 09:38.570
What a shoddy report.

09:38.740 --> 09:39.360
Rewrite it.

09:45.620 --> 09:47.160
I smell a beast...

09:48.160 --> 09:49.290
What about a beast?

09:52.960 --> 09:53.830
What's wrong?

09:54.670 --> 09:55.670
Sasamori-dono?

10:37.680 --> 10:41.850
According to Nagamimi-san,
the house Ogin-san born in should be...

10:42.310 --> 10:43.470
somewhere around here.

10:44.310 --> 10:49.310
[Sign: Restaurant]

10:49.940 --> 10:53.900
Yes, I've heard about the
robbery that happened fifteen years ago.

10:54.230 --> 10:57.700
The burglarized shop went bankrupt because of that.

10:58.200 --> 10:59.360
Isn't that right, dear?

10:59.700 --> 11:04.120
That's right. They caught the robber soon
afterwards and chopped off his head, though.

11:04.910 --> 11:07.160
That must've been Giemon's first beheading.

11:08.870 --> 11:14.460
If I remember correctly, the wife, who was
killed, had a daughter whose father was unknown.

11:16.470 --> 11:17.470
Ogin-san?

11:17.840 --> 11:21.640
However, we moved here after
the incident, so we don't know the details.

11:22.260 --> 11:26.720
Granny Ofuji, who worked next
door until last year, would know,

11:27.180 --> 11:30.480
but she went back to live with
her family in Numabukuro, so...

11:35.280 --> 11:40.030
People sometimes have pasts they don't want known.

11:41.320 --> 11:42.280
Mataichi-san!

11:44.490 --> 11:53.710
[Note: Danzaemon - hereditary title given to the official in charge
of administrating affairs for social outcasts during the Edo period.]

11:44.490 --> 11:50.750
Giemon of Inarizaka, you see, was originally
a subordinate of Danzaemon-sama in Asakusa.

11:51.040 --> 11:53.710
Giemon used to be the Kuji Inn's steward.

11:54.210 --> 12:05.010
[Note: Mushukunin - social outcasts who have been
deleted from the registry and have no rights.]

11:54.210 --> 11:57.880
The Kuji Inn... that's where they
look after the mushukunin, isn't it?

11:58.170 --> 12:05.010
Yes, if you become a steward there, learning the
mushukunin's secrets and weaknesses would be easy.

12:05.810 --> 12:11.020
He took advantage of that fact and
made the mushukunin do evil deeds.

12:12.100 --> 12:15.940
Then Giemon's underlings were
threatened into doing things against their will?

12:16.320 --> 12:20.860
Yes. When Giemon was alive, he was above the law.

12:21.280 --> 12:24.410
He reveled in his greed and
gorged on what he took from others.

12:25.200 --> 12:28.540
That is why he has not been able to
cast aside his evil obsessions, even in death,

12:28.750 --> 12:31.710
and become a monster like the Kowai.

12:32.460 --> 12:33.290
The Kowai?

12:33.960 --> 12:38.000
If you're possessed by a
Kowai, you yourself become a Kowai.

12:38.590 --> 12:41.220
There is only one way to escape this fate.

12:43.130 --> 12:48.860
Konoeya

12:43.130 --> 12:48.860
Konoeya

13:09.490 --> 13:15.420
Oh... one of your acquaintances
suffers from such a strange disease?

13:15.790 --> 13:16.790
Yes.

13:16.920 --> 13:19.210
This is about a friend of mine.

13:19.300 --> 13:23.010
There is a Chinese legend where a man
believed so strongly that he had become a beast

13:23.380 --> 13:28.050
that he really turned into one.

13:28.260 --> 13:30.390
A mental illness, perhaps?

13:30.560 --> 13:33.270
If not, the doing of a mononoke.

13:33.350 --> 13:35.390
Impossible, there's no such thing.

13:35.520 --> 13:37.360
Oh, that's right.

13:37.480 --> 13:43.530
If it's all right with you, I happen to know
a person who knows much of these matters...

13:44.030 --> 13:44.610
What?

13:53.250 --> 13:56.830
Mr. Retiree, there's an official
outside who says he wants to see you.

13:56.920 --> 13:59.210
Have you done something wrong?

14:01.540 --> 14:03.060
Ikomaya

14:01.540 --> 14:03.060
Candles

14:13.680 --> 14:17.060
If this continues, we'll stay under Boss
Giemon's control for the rest of our lives.

14:17.520 --> 14:18.850
What should we do?

14:24.650 --> 14:28.870
There's a way to ensure that a
Kowai will not come back to life.

14:32.540 --> 14:34.410
Are you clear, Momosuke-dono?

14:34.450 --> 14:36.790
This is to be kept an absolute secret.

14:36.780 --> 14:37.650
Ikomaya

14:37.210 --> 14:39.540
Of course, Sasamori-sama.

14:37.650 --> 14:38.410
Ikomaya

14:39.880 --> 14:42.840
However, it is true, right? The method you spoke of.

14:43.260 --> 14:46.720
Who knows? It is just something I heard from someone.

14:57.590 --> 15:00.330
Ikomaya

14:58.060 --> 14:58.770
Are we there yet?

14:59.190 --> 15:00.350
We're almost there.

15:03.650 --> 15:04.230
This is the place?

15:04.570 --> 15:06.570
You, wait here!

15:14.200 --> 15:15.290
It itches...

15:17.620 --> 15:20.540
There is but one way to escape the curse of the Kowai.

15:21.340 --> 15:25.760
Purify your body in the sacred spring that
wells forth in the small shrine at the end of Inarizaka.

15:27.800 --> 15:28.880
Is that it?

15:48.150 --> 15:49.780
It's been a long time since we've last met.

15:50.240 --> 15:50.950
What?

15:51.200 --> 15:51.740
Woman!

15:51.910 --> 15:52.780
Who are you?

15:54.740 --> 15:57.040
Have you forgotten now that fifteen years have passed?

15:57.910 --> 16:00.500
The face of the woman you killed...

16:00.830 --> 16:01.460
What?

16:25.270 --> 16:28.860
That mole on your forehead... I'll never forget it.

16:29.190 --> 16:30.280
Y-You can't be...

16:30.820 --> 16:31.570
that girl when I...

16:31.860 --> 16:33.160
That's impossible!

16:33.490 --> 16:36.530
How dare you... kill me?

16:36.740 --> 16:39.000
Damn you, accursed demon!

16:50.590 --> 16:51.340
Prepare yourself]

17:09.900 --> 17:12.900
C-Could it be that... this water?

17:13.860 --> 17:15.410
Which of us is the demon?

17:16.120 --> 17:19.160
Giemon of Inari, you see, isn't human.

17:20.040 --> 17:21.700
It is a setup.

17:22.080 --> 17:23.080
A "setup"?

17:23.750 --> 17:27.630
The real Giemon-san was Ogin's real father...

17:28.170 --> 17:29.250
What did you say?!

17:30.090 --> 17:35.760
However, there was a man who profited from
threatening the mushukunin in Giemon-san's name.

17:36.850 --> 17:41.640
Giemon-san tried to reveal that man's identity
to the Shogun, but instead was caught in a trap.

17:43.640 --> 17:46.190
He killed Ogin's mother and blamed Giemon-san for it.

17:46.730 --> 17:52.740
He used poison to make Giemon-san look like
a monster so he couldn't defend himself properly,

17:52.950 --> 17:57.200
and sent him off to be beheaded.

17:58.910 --> 18:02.330
In other words, Giemon was the scapegoat.

18:03.040 --> 18:05.830
He stole Giemon's head and brought him back to "life."

18:06.540 --> 18:08.580
He made Giemon into an immortal monster of sorts.

18:09.250 --> 18:11.500
The mushukunin were very surprised.

18:12.090 --> 18:15.840
Orders continued to be given by
Giemon, who was supposedly dead.

18:16.550 --> 18:18.890
There was no greater fear for them than that.

18:19.100 --> 18:22.600
Then, the other two times
"Giemon" had his head cut off...

18:23.020 --> 18:25.640
Fear lessens as time goes by.

18:26.190 --> 18:30.610
There was probably a need to prove
once in a while that Giemon was immortal.

18:31.230 --> 18:33.860
The setup didn't need to change, after all.

18:37.160 --> 18:39.780
But this time, we struck first.

18:40.450 --> 18:44.540
We stole the head before he did, and spread those rumors.

18:44.870 --> 18:45.450
I get it now...

18:46.370 --> 18:53.210
Then that kitsunebi was to let Ogin-san find
her enemy from among those who were lured there!

18:53.800 --> 18:55.420
Sasamori Kinzou.

18:56.010 --> 18:59.640
When it first began, he was an
official who frequented the Kuji Inn.

19:00.300 --> 19:04.970
Well, let's just say that he was in a perfect
position to learn the mushukunins weaknesses.

19:27.460 --> 19:28.330
Take that!

19:28.750 --> 19:29.870
You monster!

19:53.440 --> 19:54.900
What in the world is going on?

20:05.240 --> 20:07.870
The deed is done.

20:14.380 --> 20:16.630
They're off to go burn him.

20:17.260 --> 20:19.470
It's to prevent him from coming back to life.

20:38.280 --> 20:40.530
You're lucky, you know that?

20:41.280 --> 20:48.580
Since the world of humanity is a living hell,
it's better if you get to wear something pretty.

20:49.200 --> 20:51.160
See? You're all pretty now.

20:51.460 --> 20:53.420
Osame, can you help out here for a second?

20:53.710 --> 20:54.630
Right!

20:55.380 --> 20:56.920
Try to do it yourself next time.

20:58.670 --> 21:01.010
In the end, this is a transient world.

21:01.930 --> 21:03.010
Even so...

21:11.890 --> 21:13.190
Live to your utmost.

21:22.150 --> 21:23.320
Yes, yes.

21:23.570 --> 21:27.120
I remember that time well.

21:27.280 --> 21:28.490
Really?

21:28.740 --> 21:31.250
Was that five years ago?

21:31.370 --> 21:33.920
No, fifteen...

21:34.210 --> 21:37.540
It was truly a hot and humid summer night...

21:37.630 --> 21:39.710
Or, perhaps it was spring...

21:39.880 --> 21:45.550
A young girl was killed, along with her poor mother...

21:45.640 --> 21:46.090
What?

21:46.720 --> 21:50.560
She was a pretty little thing, barely ten years old.

21:50.640 --> 21:54.020
She was very fond of me, too.

21:54.190 --> 21:55.140
That's...

21:55.440 --> 21:57.060
The daughter shouldn't have died!

21:57.360 --> 21:59.070
Are you sure about this?

21:59.360 --> 22:02.150
What? Who did you say died?

22:02.320 --> 22:04.280
What a rude fellow.

22:04.400 --> 22:06.780
I have no intentions of dying just yet!

22:07.320 --> 22:11.080
Why, just yesterday, they were
nagging me to get married already...

22:14.630 --> 22:20.720
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:22.070 --> 22:28.160
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:29.140 --> 22:34.910
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:34.950 --> 22:41.580
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:42.950 --> 22:48.890
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:48.930 --> 22:55.590
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:56.430 --> 23:05.900
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:07.210 --> 23:10.410
Draw near

23:10.680 --> 23:17.680
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:17.720 --> 23:23.660
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:25.830 --> 23:31.100
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:31.140 --> 23:39.770
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:48.730 --> 23:53.910
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:54.530 --> 23:57.070
The light is envious; envious is the light.

23:57.530 --> 23:59.620
The hatred of the woman
who is in the shadows runs deep.

23:59.950 --> 24:00.580
Arson,

24:00.910 --> 24:02.960
murder, blackmail, and extortion...

24:03.040 --> 24:04.460
To sully the light...

24:04.710 --> 24:06.210
If it is to accomplish that...

24:06.670 --> 24:10.710
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:11.090 --> 24:12.130
Hinoenma

24:12.590 --> 24:14.840
The deed is done.
